If You provide a Modified Version to people outside Your legal organization
as a network service, You must offer those users the same free access to its
Corresponding Source through a conspicuous link in the service. Network
services must also comply with section 3. You need not disclose private
modifications when no copy or network service is offered to others.

Source download links must remain available while the relevant version is
distributed or operated and for at least three years after You last provided
that version. Giving the Corresponding Source with every distributed copy
satisfies the distribution source obligation without an ongoing download
link. A link only to an unmodified upstream repository is insufficient when
Your distributed or running version contains modifications.

